# Real production secrets/certs never belong in git — only the .example
# template above is tracked. Copy it to .env.production, fill in real values,
# and transfer it to the server out-of-band (scp, a secrets manager, etc.).
.env.production

# In case a real cert/key ever gets dropped here for reference — it shouldn't,
# Let's Encrypt certs live in /etc/letsencrypt on the server, not in the repo.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
